Hi again,
It appears that I got a step or 2 ahead of myself with the previous question and have run into some challenges in creating the inla.spde2 object from the barrier mesh. As before, here is the code used to create the mesh and determine which triangles should be incorporated into the barrier (i.e., the land surrounding the river where sampling took place).

max.edge <- 100000
MSR.bdry2 <- as.inla.mesh.segment(MSR_ShapeFile_UTM2)

mesh9.5 <- inla.mesh.2d(boundary = MSR.bdry2,
                        max.edge = c(1, 2) * max.edge,
                        cutoff = 50)

river.tri <- inla.over_sp_mesh(MSR_ShapeFile_UTM2,
                               y = mesh9.5,
                               type = 'centroid',
                               ignore.CRS = T)

num.tri <- length(mesh9.5$graph$tv[, 1])
barrier.tri <- setdiff(1:num.tri, river.tri)

poly.barrier <- inla.barrier.polygon(mesh9.5,
                                     barrier.triangles = barrier.tri)

I then set the pc priors and attempt to create the inla.spde2 object.

Range0      <- 5000
AlphaRange0 <- 0.05
Sigma0      <- 2.5
AlphaSigma0 <- 0.05

spde2.barrier <- inla.barrier.pcmatern(mesh2,
                                       barrier.triangles = barrier.tri,
                                       prior.range = c(Range0, AlphaRange0),
                                       prior.sigma = c(Sigma0, AlphaSigma0),
                                       range.fraction = 0.1)

When I run the inla.barrier.pcmatern() function, I get this error:

Error in if (any(i < 0L)) { : missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed
