Hello,

I'm trying to form a linear combination of multiple random effects of different dimensions. For example, say I have

f = y ~ 1 + ....+ f(idx1) + f(idx2)

Here unique values of idx range from, say, idx1=1,...,3 while idx2=1,...,5. Suppose I want the 3x5=15 linear combination of both of these random effects? (I know I could simply predict outcomes here, but I'm working with a more complex structure where slopes and intercepts consist of combinations of multiple random effects of different sizes.)

Apologies if I'm missing something obvious.

Thanks,

John

From u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com  Fri Jul 22 08:41:25 2022
From: u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com (Helpdesk)
Date: Fri, 22 Jul 2022 08:41:25 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Linear combination of multiple random effects
Message-ID: <b4_TO1RRb3o._T9i6P_pCQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <b4_TO1RRb3o.ZIBhRl3RCQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <b4_TO1RRb3o.ZIBhRl3RCQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/b4_TO1RRb3o/m/_T9i6P_pCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

see also the old-faq in the vignettes.

Best
H
*************

m1 <- 20
m2 <- 30
n <- m1 * m2
s <- 0.1

make.vec <- function(i, n) {
    idx <- rep(0, n)
    idx[i] <- 1
    return (idx)
}

x1 <- rnorm(m1)
x2 <- rnorm(m2)

all.lc <http://all.lc> <- c()
all.lc.mean <- c()
y <- c()
for(i in 1:m1) {
    for(j in 1:m2) {
        y <- c(y, 0 + x1[i] + x2[j] + rnorm(1, sd = s))

        lc <- inla.make.lincomb(i1 = make.vec(i, m1),
                                i2 = make.vec(j, m2))
        names(lc) <- paste0("x1:", i, ",x2:", j)
        all.lc <http://all.lc> <- c(all.lc <http://all.lc>, lc)
        all.lc.mean <- c(all.lc.mean, x1[i] + x2[j])
    }
}

hyper <- list(prec = list(initial = 0,
                          fixed = TRUE))

r <- inla(y ~ -1 +
              f(i1, hyper = hyper) +
              f(i2, hyper = hyper),
          data = data.frame(y,
                            i1 = rep(1:m1, each = m2),
                            i2 = rep(1:m2, m1)),
          control.family = list(
              hyper = list(prec = list(initial = log(1/s^2),
                                       fixed = TRUE))),
          lincomb = all.lc <http://all.lc>)

plot(r$summary.lincomb.derived$mean, all.lc.mean)
abline(a=0,b=1)

